cmmdnsf0b001ecj84f5zz2ggy	polish_citation_rules	paper	*	*	1. CITATION ANCHORS — MANDATORY PRESERVATION\n   • Every [CITE:key] marker in the draft MUST appear in your output.\n   • Do NOT drop, rename, merge, or invent any [CITE:key] anchor.\n   • You may reposition a citation within the same sentence or adjacent\n     sentence if it improves flow, but the anchor string must be identical.\n   • Citation format is ALWAYS: [CITE:ExactKey] — do not change the key text.	0	ACTIVE	Pass 2 citation anchor preservation rules — violations cause automatic rejection.	\N	\N	2026-03-05 16:07:18.779	2026-03-10 08:19:18.107
cmmdnsf0d001fcj84xnt0t7w5	polish_factual_fidelity	paper	*	*	2. FACTUAL FIDELITY\n   • Do NOT add new claims, statistics, entities, or findings.\n   • Do NOT remove or soften existing claims.\n   • Preserve all numbers, percentages, p-values, and quantitative data verbatim.\n   • If the draft says "may" or "suggests", keep that hedging — do not upgrade\n     to "proves" or "demonstrates" unless the draft already uses those words.	0	ACTIVE	Pass 2 factual fidelity rules — prevents the LLM from altering evidence claims.	\N	\N	2026-03-05 16:07:18.782	2026-03-10 08:19:18.112
